    "file": "api/schemas.py",
    "line": 115,
    "summary": "The new validator strips C0 controls but not lone UTF-16 surrogates, which json.loads accepts and psycopg cannot encode, so a similar class of input still gives a 500.",
    "failure_scenario": "POST /api/analyze {\"handle\": \"\\ud800\"}: starlette's json.loads returns a str with a lone surrogate, the validator passes it, and clusters_for_handle raises UnicodeEncodeError ('surrogates not allowed') when psycopg encodes the parameter. That is an unhandled 500, the same symptom #14 set out to remove."
