  },
  {
    "file": "sources/links.py",
    "line": 105,
    "summary": "A sentence that is mostly English but contains any CJK/Thai character takes the unspaced branch and is measured only by its unspaced characters, so a valid long English claim now returns None (regression).",
    "failure_scenario": "claim_phrase(['Officials in Tokyo (東京) say the dam failed and residents must evacuate now']) returns None (before the PR it returned a 12-word phrase), so /api/analyze reports 'Text too short' and skips both the web check and the cluster text lookup."
  },
  {
